<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Scheut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1356</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-brabantine-succession">War of the Brabantine Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Scheut was fought on 17 August 1356 at Scheut, near Anderlecht west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-brabantine-succession">War of the Brabantine Succession</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-count-of-flanders">Louis of Male</a>, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, defeated the army of Duchess Joanna and Duke Wenceslaus of Brabant and occupied Brussels and other towns. Brussels was recaptured that October by a small force led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/everard-tserclaes">Everard t'Serclaes</a>, and the Peace of Ath in 1357 left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> to Flanders.</p></div>
